s better, but we need to consider A's strengths. Or we could shift recommendation if we think A is better. But we need to be evidence-based. B has strong reliability and stress handling, but communication concerns. A has 100% reliability and positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric. Which is more critical? Probably communication is crucial. B's communication issues are pretentious and wrong tone, but maybe can be mitigated. A's difficulty communicating ideas may be more severe. So we can argue B remains best. Provide comparison.\n\nThus our public message: \"I agree with the earlier recommendation of B, but I'd like to bring Candidate A into the discussion to ensure coverage. While A is 100% reliable and creates a positive atmosphere, his difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric attitude raise concerns for crew cooperation and professional communication, especially on long-haul flights. Compared to B, A lacks demonstrated stress resilience and technical competence (weather assessment, computer skills). Therefore B still appears the stronger overall fit.\" Also include vote remains Candidate B.\n\nWe need to include METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B.\n\nLet's produce that."}
